[
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have something like this already?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousSesquilinearForm</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RCLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"bp\">⋆</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"bp\">⋆</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I am trying to put an inner product on a tangent space.</p>",
        "id": 614764993,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1785936730
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ContinuousLinearMap.bilinearComp#doc\">docs#ContinuousLinearMap.bilinearComp</a> maybe?</p>",
        "id": 614767982,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1785937544
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've also thought about this question (as I'm supervising a student who is defining the standard hyperbolic metric on the Poincaré disk). The above is the best we have, but also not a full answer (and I'm not sure what's the most elegant solution, yet).</p>",
        "id": 614796625,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1785944887
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The issue is that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=TangentSpace#doc\">docs#TangentSpace</a> is not a normed space, so <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ContinuousLInearMap.bilinearComp#doc\">docs#ContinuousLInearMap.bilinearComp</a> does not apply. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearMap.bilinearComp#doc\">docs#LinearMap.bilinearComp</a> does (which gives you just linear maps each time), and then you can manually upgrade these to be continuous linear (or use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LinearMap.continuous_of_finiteDimensional#doc\">docs#LinearMap.continuous_of_finiteDimensional</a>). I think a version of <code>bilinearComp</code> where the target is just a TVS, but we have finite-dimensionality, would be useful.</p>",
        "id": 614797017,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1785944995
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(The other option is to locally define a bad norm on the tangent space and apply <code>ContinuousLinearMap.bilinearComp</code>). I haven't made up my mind up yet if I find this better or worse. What do you think, Kevin and Sébastien?)</p>",
        "id": 614797102,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1785945020
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think we should have a typeclass <code>NormableSpace</code> and use it there.</p>",
        "id": 614803976,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1785947033
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Indeed. Perhaps it's a bit surprising that we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=PolynormableSpace#doc\">docs#PolynormableSpace</a> but not <code>NormableSpace</code> <span aria-label=\"smiley\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f603\" role=\"img\" title=\"smiley\">:smiley:</span></p>",
        "id": 614821777,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1785952352
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have thought about creating such a typeclass, but then there is the question whether we want to have a <code>Normable(Add)Group</code> typeclass for <code>Normed(Add)Group</code>, which would involve generalizing quite a bit of the <code>WithSeminorms</code> machinery to <code>(Add)GroupSeminorm</code> and that would be quite an effort and I don't know whether it is worth it.</p>",
        "id": 614877512,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1785975517
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And for <code>NormableRing</code> as well I guess. We get in trouble for <code>NormableModule</code>, since we can't translate <code>[NormedAddCommGroup M] [NormedSpace R M] [NormedSpace S M]</code> into the <code>Normable</code> mechanism since there's no way to state the norms are all the same.</p>",
        "id": 614878289,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785975741
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, I didn't know that there is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RingSeminorm#doc\">docs#RingSeminorm</a> (I am highly confused by the folder structure - why is <code>GroupSeminorm</code> in <code>Normed/Group/Seminorm</code>, but <code>RingSeminorm</code> in <code>Normed/Unbundled/RingSeminorm</code>? I have a PR moving <code>Seminorm.lean</code> to <code>Normed/Seminorm/Basic.lean</code>, but maybe we should have all of the unbundled seminorm files in <code>Seminorm/(Group/Ring/Module)/Something.lean</code>?)</p>",
        "id": 614880170,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Doll",
        "timestamp": 1785977258
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"634338\">Michael Rothgang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Pulling.20back.20continuous.20inner.20product/near/614797017\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The issue is that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=TangentSpace#doc\">docs#TangentSpace</a> is not a normed space</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I would add that the tangent space <em>is</em> a normed space in the case of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsRiemannianManifold#doc\">docs#IsRiemannianManifold</a> (as one might expect), or under the weaker condition that the tangent space is a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RiemannianBundle#doc\">docs#RiemannianBundle</a>--I suspect this may be relevant to the project Kevin is supervising. For example, the following code compiles:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bornology</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Manifold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Filter</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ENNReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContDiff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ModelWithCorners</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"n\">ω</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ChartedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">RiemannianBundle</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> A normed space structure on the tangent space -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TangentSpace</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 615748191,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1786410916
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42983\">#42983</a> introduces a class <code>IsNormableSpace</code> and provides basic API around it.</p>\n<p>I think <code>NormableSpace</code> is very different from <code>NormableRing</code>, say: typically, analysis will work with topological vector spaces over a normed field. So the question of whether rings or fields are normable is not really important (typically, they already come with a norm), while the same question for vector spaces is very important. So, the PR only does <code>IsNormableSpace</code> and not the other ones.</p>",
        "id": 617942256,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1787322138
    }
]